g/","score":3,"flags":0,"comment_count":1,"description":"\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href=\"https://adepts.of0x.cc/eufy-homestation2-firmware/\" rel=\"ugc\"\u003eHere is the follow-up dive into the base station\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n","description_plain":"[Here is the follow-up dive into the base station](https://adepts.of0x.cc/eufy-homestation2-firmware/)","submitter_user":"hoistbypetard","user_is_author":false,"tags":["hardware","security"],"short_id_url":"https://lobste.rs/s/e84scc","comments_url":"https://lobste.rs/s/e84scc/hacking_eufy_doorbell_base_station"},{"short_id":"u9ue6c","created_at":"2026-10-11T04:37:56.100-05:00","title":"What's Wrong with GitHub","url":"https://www.gnu.org/philosophy/whats-wrong-with-github.html","score":51,"flags":2,"comment_count":43,"description":"","description_plain":"","submitter_user":"tusharhero","user_is_author":false,"tags":["vcs"],"short_id_url":"https://lobste.rs/s/u9ue6c","comments_url":"https://lobste.rs/s/u9ue6c/what_s_wrong_with_github"},{"short_id":"9wcfld","created_at":"2026-10-11T04:25:42.986-05:00","title":"How big is a Git commit?","url":"https://ratfactor.com/cards/git-commit-size","score":29,"flags":0,"comment_count":3,"description":"","description_plain":"","submitter_user":"rajtilakjee","user_is_author":false,"tags":["vcs"],"short_id_url":"https://lobste.rs/s/9wcfld","comments_url":"https://lobste.rs/s/9wcfld/how_big_is_git_commit"},{"short_id":"7mllxi","created_at":"2026-10-11T01:21:34.089-05:00","title":"JSON Tiles: Fast Analytics on Semi-Structured Data (2021)","url":"https://db.cit.tum.de/~durner/papers/json-tiles-sigmod21.pdf","score":3,"flags":0,"comment_count":0,"description":"\u003cp\u003eAbstract: Developers often prefer flexibility over upfront schema design, making semi-structured data formats such as JSON increasingly popular. Large amounts of JSON data are therefore stored and analyzed by\nrelational database systems. In existing systems, however, JSON’s lack of a fixed schema results in slow analytics. In this paper, we present JSON tiles, which, without losing the flexibility of JSON, enables relational systems to perform analytics on JSON data at native speed. JSON tiles automatically detects the most important keys and\nextracts them transparently – often achieving scan performance similar to columnar storage. At the same time, JSON tiles is capable of handling heterogeneous and changing data. Furthermore, we\nautomatically collect statistics that enable the query optimizer to find good execution plans. Our experimental evaluation compares against state-of-the-art systems and research proposals and shows that our approach is both robust and efficient.\u003c/p\u003e\n","description_plain":"Abstract: Developers often prefer flexibility over upfront schema design, making semi-structured data formats such as JSON increasingly popular. Large amounts of JSON data are therefore stored and analyzed by\r\nrelational database systems. In existing systems, however, JSON’s lack of a fixed schema results in slow analytics. In this paper, we present JSON tiles, which, without losing the flexibility of JSON, enables relational systems to perform analytics on JSON data at native speed. JSON tiles automatically detects the most important keys and\r\nextracts them transparently – often achieving scan performance similar to columnar storage. At the same time, JSON tiles is capable of handling heterogeneous and changing data. Furthermore, we\r\nautomatically collect statistics that enable the query optimizer to find good execution plans. Our experimental evaluation compares against state-of-the-art systems and research proposals and shows that our approach is both robust and efficient.","submitter_user":"typesanitizer","user_is_author":false,"tags":["databases","pdf","performance"],"short_id_url":"https://lobste.rs/s/7mllxi","comments_url":"https://lobste.rs/s/7mllxi/json_tiles_fast_analytics_on_semi"},{"short_id":"ecxril","created_at":"2026-10-11T01:21:25.386-05:00","title":"LineageOS 24.0 released","url":"https://lineageos.org/Changelog-32/","score":37,"flags":0,"comment_count":14,"description":"","description_plain":"","submitter_user":"timschumi","user_is_author":false,"tags":["android","mobile","release"],"short_id_url":"https://lobste.rs/s/ecxril","comments_url":"https://lobste.rs/s/ecxril/lineageos_24_0_released"},{"short_id":"6vjx1k","created_at":"2026-10-11T01:16:26.688-05:00","title":"How shredding JSON is giving Logfire 1000x query speedups","url":"https://pydantic.dev/articles/dynamic-shredding-2026-01-26","score":20,"flags":0,"comment_count":3,"description":"","description_plain":"","submitter_user":"typesanitizer","user_is_author":false,"tags":["databases","performance"],"short_id_url":"https://lobste.rs/s/6vjx1k","comments_url":"https://lobste.rs/s/6vjx1k/how_shredding_json_is_giving_logfire"},{"short_id":"rhy5zp","created_at":"2026-10-10T19:51:28.569-05:00","title":"Consistency is not a localized property","url":"https://n-the-loop.com/blog/consistency-is-not-a-localized-property/","score":10,"flags":1,"comment_count":6,"description":"","description_plain":"","submitter_user":"b--man","user_is_author":true,"tags":["ai","databases","programming"],"short_id_url":"https://lobste.rs/s/rhy5zp","comments_url":"https://lobste.rs/s/rhy5zp/consistency_is_not_localized_property"},{"short_id":"fbs3k7","created_at":"2026-10-10T18:25:51.517-05:00","title":"Making np.searchsorted up to 25× Faster in NumPy 2.5","url":"https://blog.scientific-python.org/numpy/searchsorted/","score":11,"flags":0,"comment_count":19,"description":"","description_plain":"","submitter_user":"itamarst","user_is_author":false,"tags":["performance"],"short_id_url":"https://lobste.rs/s/fbs3k7","comments_url":"https://lobste.rs/s/fbs3k7/making_np_searchsorted_up_25x_faster"}]